---
import { asset, site } from "../lib/data";
import { highlightDiff, highlightSource } from "../scripts/highlight";

const data = site();
const lint = data.lint;
const finding = lint.before.findings[0];
const fixDiff = lint.diff.split("\n").filter((l: string) => !l.startsWith("---") && !l.startsWith("+++")).join("\n");
const clay = `parts:
  - capsule: { from: [0, 0.32, 0], to: [0, 0.74, 0], radius: 0.3 }
    color: red                      # a palette name
  - capsule: { from: [0.3, 0.6, 0], to: [0.42, 0.38, 0.08], radius: 0.08 }
    id: arm_l
    mirror: x                       # write the left one...
    mirror_id: arm_r                # ...the right is its own part
    blend: 0.04                     # melts into the body, like clay
  - box: { at: [0, 0.56, 0.29], size: [0.09, 0.22, 0.05], round: 0.015 }
    pattern: { type: stripes, color: gold, size: 0.06, axis: y }
  - cylinder: { at: [0, 0.81, 0], radius: 0.26, height: 0.04 }
    cut: true                       # holes and openings`;
const rig = `rig:
  arm: { pivot: [0, 1.78, 0], meta: { fires: true } }
skin: rigid                  # or soft: one mesh that bends
animations:
  fire:
    fps: 12
    loop: false
    poses:
      - {}
      - { arm: { rotate: [35, 0, 0] } }
      - { arm: { rotate: [80, 0, 0] } }
      - { arm: { rotate: [120, 0, 0] } }
  # or a cycle: walk, waddle, hop, bob, spin,
  # swing, breathe, wave, chain`;
const pilot = data.models.pilot;
const manifest = JSON.stringify(
  {
    pilot: {
      glb: "models/pilot.glb",
      scene: "models/pilot.tscn",
      height: pilot.height,
      triangles: pilot.triangles.soft_toy,
      parts: { cap: { pivot: [0, 1, 0], meta: { detachable: true } }, "…": `${pilot.parts - 1} more` },
      animations: { walk: { loop: true, fps: 12 }, "…": `${Object.keys(pilot.animations).length - 1} more` },
      variants: pilot.variants,
    },
  },
  null,
  1,
).replace(/\[\n\s*([^\[\]{}]*?)\n\s*\]/g, (_, s: string) => `[${s.replace(/\s*\n\s*/g, " ")}]`);
const gd = `add_child(load("res://assets/kiln/looks/soft_toy.tscn").instantiate())  # once per scene
var pilot = load("res://assets/kiln/models/pilot.tscn").instantiate()
add_child(pilot)
pilot.get_node("AnimationPlayer").play("wave")`;
---

<section id="features">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="eyebrow">Why KILN</span>
    <h2>Built for a whole game's worth of models</h2>
    <p class="lede">
      Every picture below is KILN's own output, from the demo project in this site's repository: its previews,
      its lint, its build.
    </p>

    <div class="cards">
      <article class="card wide">
        <div class="text">
          <h3><span>1</span> Shapes that blend like clay</h3>
          <p>
            Eleven primitives (spheres, capsules, rounded boxes, cylinders, cones, tori, tubes, lathes, extrusions,
            wedges) that join smoothly where you ask, cut each other, mirror and repeat in rows and rings. Colours
            are palette names; stripes, bands, dots and checks have clean edges; PAGAN images go on as decals.
          </p>
          <p class="dim">Text the agent writes and you can read, diff and review in a pull request.</p>
        </div>
        <pre class="code"><code set:html={highlightSource(clay)} /></pre>
      </article>

      <article class="card">
        <h3><span>2</span> It looks at its own work</h3>
        <p>
          Previews render on any machine, no GPU or display: a turntable from 8 sides and 3 heights, close-ups of
          any part, animation filmstrips, a line-up at one scale. The skill tells the agent to look before it
          reports, because nobody judges proportions blind.
        </p>
        <a href={asset("img/knight-turntable.png")}><img src={asset("img/knight-turntable.png")} alt="KILN's turntable of the knight: 8 sides from below, eye level and above" loading="lazy" /></a>
      </article>

      <article class="card">
        <h3><span>3</span> It checks its own work</h3>
        <p>A linter for 3D: floating pieces, parts too thin to mesh, models off the ground, wrong size for the class, blown triangle budgets. A real one, from the archer's first draft:</p>
        <p class="find"><b>{finding.rule}</b> {finding.message}</p>
        <div class="pair">
          <figure><img src={asset("img/archer-before.png")} alt="The archer's first draft: the bow floats beside the hand" loading="lazy" /><figcaption>draft</figcaption></figure>
          <figure><img src={asset("img/archer-after.png")} alt="Fixed: the bow is in the archer's hand" loading="lazy" /><figcaption>fixed: {lint.after.warnings} warnings</figcaption></figure>
        </div>
        <pre class="code small"><code set:html={highlightDiff(fixDiff)} /></pre>
      </article>

      <article class="card wide">
        <div class="text">
          <h3><span>4</span> Rigs and animation</h3>
          <p>
            Give a part an id and a pivot and it moves. Rigid skins for machines and props; soft skins for
            creatures, one mesh that bends where its parts blend. Write poses frame by frame, or let a cycle write
            them. Gameplay data rides along: <code>meta: {"{"} hitzone: head {"}"}</code> becomes node metadata in
            the engine.
          </p>
          <pre class="code"><code set:html={highlightSource(rig)} /></pre>
        </div>
        <img src={asset("img/trebuchet-fire.png")} alt="KILN's filmstrip of the trebuchet's fire animation, front and side" loading="lazy" />
      </article>

      <article class="card wide">
        <div class="text">
          <h3><span>5</span> Game-ready output</h3>
          <p>
            <code>kiln build</code> writes binary glTF (.glb) with parts, skins, animations, variants and LODs,
            within the style's triangle budget. For Godot: a scene per model with the style's materials (toon
            bands, outlines, rim light) and a look kit per style (sky, sun, tonemapper, SSAO, glow). <code>kiln
            build --verify-godot</code> loads it all in headless Godot. <code>manifest.json</code> is the contract
            for any engine.
          </p>
          <pre class="code"><code set:html={highlightSource(gd)} /></pre>
        </div>
        <div>
          <img src={asset("img/godot-showcase.png")} alt="The demo models running in Godot 4 with the soft_toy look kit" loading="lazy" />
          <pre class="code small"><code>{manifest}</code></pre>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="card">
        <h3><span>6</span> Everything at one scale</h3>
        <p>
          Models are written in metres. <code>kiln lineup</code> stands them on one ground line beside a 1 m bar,
          so a 1.2 m bean doesn't end up taller than the door. Lint W108 flags sizes that don't fit their class.
        </p>
        <img src={asset("img/lineup.png")} alt="KILN's line-up: pilot, passenger, knight, archer, barrel, seat and tree at one scale" loading="lazy" />
      </article>

      <article class="card">
        <h3><span>7</span> Free asset packs, in your style</h3>
        <p>
          Text is bad at dense foliage and realistic rocks. For those, bring in CC0 packs (Kenney, KayKit,
          Quaternius): KILN scales them, stands them on the ground, snaps their colours to your palette and gives
          them your style's materials, so they match. <code>CREDITS.md</code> writes itself.
        </p>
        <pre class="code"><code><span class="t-punc">$</span> kiln import rock.glb --licence CC0-1.0 \
    --author Kenney --height 1.5</code></pre>
        <p class="dim">Licences that forbid it (NC, ND, "no AI") are refused by the skill.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="card">
        <h3><span>8</span> A project that remembers</h3>
        <p>
          <code>BRIEF.md</code> (what the game needs, every decision) and <code>STYLE.md</code> (how it looks)
          are the agent's memory between sessions. Models carry a status and a style version; <code>kiln style
          bump</code> flags older models for review, and <code>kiln status</code> lists what's left.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="card">
        <h3><span>9</span> Built for agents</h3>
        <p>
          A Claude skill that teaches the workflow, an MCP server (20 tools, previews come back as images) for any
          agent, <code>--json</code> on every command, and <code>kiln.api</code> for generator scripts: walls with
          merlons, fences, stairs, forests, crowds.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .cards {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 22px;
    margin-top: 40px;
  }
  .card {
    background: var(--panel);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: 24px;
    min-width: 0;
  }
  .card.wide {
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1.1fr);
    gap: 28px;
    align-items: start;
  }
  h3 span {
    display: inline-grid;
    place-items: center;
    width: 1.6em;
    height: 1.6em;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--clay);
    color: var(--ink);
    font-size: 0.85em;
    margin-right: 6px;
  }
  .card p {
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .dim {
    font-size: 0.92rem;
  }
  .card img {
    display: block;
    border-radius: 8px;
    margin-top: 6px;
  }
  .card .code {
    font-size: 12.5px;
  }
  .code.small {
    font-size: 11.5px;
    margin-top: 12px;
  }
  .find {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--text) !important;
    background: var(--ink);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--glow);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 10px 12px;
  }
  .find b {
    color: var(--glow);
  }
  .pair {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 10px;
  }
  .pair figure {
    margin: 0;
    background: linear-gradient(#bcd7f2, #e9f1f8);
    border-radius: 8px;
  }
  .pair figcaption {
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: #3a2c25;
    text-align: center;
    padding-bottom: 6px;
  }
  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .cards,
    .card.wide {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    }
  }
</style>
